{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/523500-1st-ed-thoughts-about-transmassion-aptitude","id":523500,"title":"[1st Ed] Thoughts about Transmassion aptitude","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-21T11:17:33-07:00","id":523500,"title":"[1st Ed] Thoughts about Transmassion aptitude","content":"Been thinking about the current (1st ed) ruling on the allowed mass you may 'port using the Transmassion aptitude.<br /> <br /> To put it simply, the book Stellar Frontier says you may transport xyz kilograms of mass, depending on your Psi rating. Or one person, no matter if a 50kg dwarf or a 150kg giant. Especially when porting objects, the mass restriction does not really make sense to me. So what could be alternatives?<br /> <br /> 1.) Volumina<br /> Instead of calculating the allowed object to be ported by <i>mass</i> (kg) per level/success/point spend/etc., it could be calculated by it's <i>volume</i> (cubic meter). Which makes sense; you don't lift the object, you instantly relocate it through space. It should be more difficult to manipulare more space, the mass involved seems not to be a factor in my eyes. Also, how do you calculate mass if you want to port something from earth or, e.g., mars, where gravity is much lower?<br /> <br /> 2.) Density<br /> This includes <i>both</i> mass and volume into the calculation. It might be easier to port a qubic meter of foam than a cubic meter of lead, simply because the density of lead is way higher. Might make sense as well, from a teleporting point of view. But to be honest, when running games you don't want to scientifically calculate density of objects (how dense is a person, btw?). So, I think I might prefer to use volume as the limiting factor for Transmassion.<br /> <br /> Btw: Why then differentiate between objects and persons at all? It simply is a bunch of mass/volume to be ported. Maybe you could give penalties for unwilling entities (be it a human or a sentient machine or ...), and/or easier when you have your psi print on that thing.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Are there already some ideas or teasers on how aptitudes like Teleporting work in the upcoming 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3122-shuragil","name":"shuragil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T12:39:52-07:00","id":523576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shuragil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think? Are there already some ideas or teasers on how aptitudes like Teleporting work in the upcoming 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just FYI there have been no mechanics teasers released on anything at all for 2nd Ed. The core 'Sardonyx' system is still being worked on (as per Monday Meeting updates in the blog). Click the link in my sig to track down the 'what we know so far' document that compiles what we've put together from various setting hints found online, in these forums etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}